Controls: CIS 7.3; NIST SI-2; ISO 8.8; CE Security update management

The security updates waiting could not be counted, because the
package manager has nothing cached to count them from: apt's package
lists are empty (container images often delete them), dnf has no
cached metadata, or zypper could not read its repositories without
refreshing them. Tigris does not refresh them itself, since that
needs the network. 'apt update', 'dnf makecache' or 'zypper refresh'
fill the cache, and the next run counts.

Auditing an offline root (--root) that is mounted read-only, dnf 4
cannot write its log there and zypper cannot rebuild its cache, so they
do not answer; the message quotes what they said. A writable copy of
the root lets them answer, writing their logs and caches into it as
they would on that system (dnf 5's log, and zypper's lock and log, are
kept out of it).
